    Spread two single-core V4.1 decode reductions over the GPU
    
    Two reductions in V4.1 decode ran on a tiny part of the GPU: the Engram gate used one 32-thread SIMD group per stream, and the hyper-connection collapse used a single threadgroup. The gate now uses eight SIMD groups per stream, and the collapse is split across 42 threadgroups in two kernels. Each thread still adds its values in the original order, so the results are bit-identical.
    
    DS4_METAL_DISABLE_V41_SPLIT_REDUCE=1 goes back to the single-group kernels.

